      "message": "nit: I struggle to explain myself here, but I find it awkward to say \"Some thing we\u0027re not doing is bad.\" My first thought was to suggest something like:\n\n```\n// Use a function to avoid a static initializer.\n```\n\nwhich *also* references what we\u0027re not doing. Maybe I think I like it better since it\u0027s at least explicit about what it\u0027s doing instead.",
