      "writtenOn": "2023-05-09T16:16:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a little concerned about this call. This will call [`BytesRequiredForIsRaw`](https://source.corp.google.com/android-internal/external/piex/src/piex.cc;l\u003d636;rcl\u003deeae447b7baf32568765801cb304d72dadfcd739), which calls [`RequestedSize`](https://source.corp.google.com/android-internal/external/piex/src/image_type_recognition/image_type_recognition_lite.cc;l\u003d60;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;rcl\u003deeae447b7baf32568765801cb304d72dadfcd739), which has implementations that go up to 5000. As I understand it, unless we use the full size, it will return `false` when it should\u0027ve returned `true`. That\u0027s why we didn\u0027t have an `IsRaw`, and why we put `SkRawCodec` last.\n\nMaybe `IsRaw` should just return `true`? We should also document somewhere that raw must be last.",
      "revId": "46a8075dcc9f0492dd6aa4497887bf3ac7701ef4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
